     ],
     "status": "proposed",
     "excerpt": "S2 currently requires corrective action and retesting above 5%, rather than an automatic market ban; preserve that distinction and avoid any language that makes exceeding 5% an automatic sales prohibition. S5 should distinguish regulator/customer notification from mandatory recall and specify how the model-level 8/100k threshold is calculated.",
     "comparison": "Proposes keeping S2's >5% corrective-action approach (weakened relative to the 5% cap) and distinguishing S5 notification from mandatory recall (weakened relative to mandatory recall at >8/100k), pairing Northwind's S2 benefit with Halcyon's S5 benefit."
    }
   ],
